{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And now come, etc.</b> The meaning of לכו is that before he reaches them, they would go out to meet him; therefore Scripture is precise in saying <b>ועתה</b> — at that very time, go. And the reason is because of the zeal and haste that they could not bear to wait until he arrived among them. Therefore you will find that they did not delay when he reached them, but immediately, as soon as he came, they did what they did. And their saying <b>ונהרגהו</b> is along the lines of what they of blessed memory said (Bava Kamma 26b): ten men who kill one man, if all of them act together, they are exempt. Therefore they contrived and said ונהרגהו together, for by this they would be exempt under human law:" "And His saying <b>ונשליכהו</b> etc. <b>ואמרנו</b> — meaning, that when we throw him into the pits, the weasels and martens commonly found in the pits will eat him, and by this we will be able to say ״חיה רעה אכלתהו״ — not that they would say ״חיה רעה הרגתהו״, and by this they do not utter a falsehood from their mouths." "<b>And if</b> you would say: on what did the tribes of YH rely to kill a human being — and all the more so the soul of a righteous man, their brother? For even though they plotted to kill him in a manner for which they would not be liable, as we have written, nevertheless they are not exempt from the judgment of Heaven, and HaShem will come in judgment." "<b>Perhaps</b> the brothers judged him by the law of a conspiring witness, for we find that he brought an evil report about them to their father and said things for which they would be liable to the death penalty based on his testimony: this one — that they ate a limb from a living animal; this one — that they were guilty of sexual immorality; and for each of these, the children of Noah are liable to death, and a son of Noah is executed on the testimony of a single witness, without warning, and on the testimony of relatives as well (Rambam, Laws of Kings, chapter 9). Therefore they judged him by the law of a conspiring witness and they are exempt from the judgments of Heaven. Only that under human law they are not exempt, for they have no formal refutation (הזמה); therefore they contrived to kill him all together, for by this there is no liability for any of them, as we have written. But under the judgment of Heaven they are exempt, for the reason that they knew with certainty that he sought to kill them. And all this was the cause within the causes to bring about what HaShem had planned. Or perhaps they alluded in their words that they would ultimately repent, and there is nothing that stands before repentance — and that is His saying <b>ועתה</b>, and they of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah, chapter 21): ואין ועתה אלא תשובה, and this is the way of derash." "<b>And we will see what will become, etc.</b> They intended to prove that he had spoken falsely in his dreams, or because his thoughts while in bed had ascended (i.e., were baseless), and the proof is that when they kill him, this will be a sign for you that he was fabricating from his own heart, or his thoughts, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:46.057766980Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}